						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, September 18, 2000</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">New voice recognition product for EverQuest users! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Did the prospect of voice recognition in EQ excite you, but Verant’s feeble attempt let you down?  Well, the solution is here, and it’s called BattleVoice!

BattleVoice is a program developed by EQ players for EQ players and it gives you exactly what you want and need in voice recognition.

First – BattleVoice comes with a recognition engine included so you don’t have to spend a ton of money on Dragon or other voice recognition packages to get it to work.

Second – BattleVoice works and works well. It’s phrase based and is completely customizable.  You can create any phrases you want or use the hundreds we included.  When you say “run to the zone!” into the microphone, that’s exactly what’s typed into your chat screen.  It was designed to relieve you from typing the things you need to say during combat, not to just save you from clicking one button.

Visit www.BattleVoice.com to learn more about the program, how it works, and how it can make your EQ game play much more user-friendly and enjoyable.

							<br>
							 - support@battlevoice.com<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=95">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, September 07, 2000</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">NEW EVERQUEST COMIC SITE </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							We just started a new everquest comic site called EVERFEAST. We have a weekly comic strip, animations featuring the dieties of the Everfeast world of NoBath, and message boards so you can leave your thoughts. Stop on by if you get a chance. The site address is www.everfeast.com

Thanks bunches,
Flab
							<br>
							 - Flab Fattius<BR><BR>
							</p>
